1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,260
Is that the Tokyo Met building?

2
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,560
That's just a regular office building.

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,820
Why? Where are you trying to go?

4
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,960
I'm heading to Tokyo City Esperion Soccer Town.

5
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,940
They're holding tryouts today.

6
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,840
I'm hoping to snag a spot on the youth team.

7
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:57,031
Ohhhh!

8
00:02:01,031 --> 00:02:04,031
All this is a soccer facility?

9
00:02:04,031 --> 00:02:06,031
It looks like a battleship!

10
00:02:13,031 --> 00:02:16,031
They must all be here for tryouts, too.

11
00:02:17,031 --> 00:02:20,031
Well, guess I better get out there and start practicing.

12
00:02:20,031 --> 00:02:23,031
Oh, right. The registration fee.

13
00:02:25,031 --> 00:02:30,031
Oh, I'm sorry.

14
00:02:40,031 --> 00:02:43,031
Are you... from Ehime?

15
00:02:43,031 --> 00:02:46,031
Uh, yeah, but what gave it away?

16
00:02:48,031 --> 00:02:49,031
All this hair.

17
00:02:49,031 --> 00:02:52,031
I was told some guy with hair like Valderamas was gonna show up.

18
00:02:52,031 --> 00:02:54,031
My brother's the one who said it, not me.

19
00:02:54,031 --> 00:02:56,031
But I'd say he's right.

20
00:02:56,031 --> 00:02:58,031
Oh, really?

21
00:02:58,031 --> 00:02:59,031
Cut that out!

22
00:02:59,031 --> 00:03:02,031
Stay out of my personal space! I don't even know you!

23
00:03:02,031 --> 00:03:03,031
Whatever.

24
00:03:03,031 --> 00:03:06,031
My bro won't shut up about you, so I don't see you as a stranger.

25
00:03:06,031 --> 00:03:09,031
It's so annoying.

26
00:03:09,031 --> 00:03:10,031
Eh?

27
00:03:11,031 --> 00:03:13,031
Come on, Hana! Hurry it up!

28
00:03:13,031 --> 00:03:15,031
We're about to get started with tryouts.

29
00:03:15,031 --> 00:03:16,031
Hey! Coming!

30
00:03:17,031 --> 00:03:19,031
Uh...

31
00:03:20,031 --> 00:03:23,031
Here for tryouts? Right this way! Follow me!

32
00:03:23,031 --> 00:03:32,031
We have a total of 86 hopefuls. I have noticed some promising candidates.

33
00:03:32,031 --> 00:03:36,031
Soichiro Tachibana from Yokoyama Musashino's junior youth soccer team.

34
00:03:36,031 --> 00:03:38,031
He's determined and strong.

35
00:03:38,031 --> 00:03:42,031
He was on the team that won the Kanto Boys soccer tournament.

36
00:03:43,031 --> 00:03:44,031
Next we have...

37
00:03:44,031 --> 00:03:45,031
Akinori Kaneda.

38
00:03:45,031 --> 00:03:49,031
He's the captain of the prestigious Tama Central junior high team.

39
00:03:49,031 --> 00:03:52,031
There's Yudai Hasegawa from Seiran junior high.

40
00:03:52,031 --> 00:03:55,031
And Lee Yong-suk, who's from Seiran as well.

41
00:03:55,031 --> 00:04:00,031
What about you? Done anything of real note, Nahime?

42
00:04:02,031 --> 00:04:03,031
Ugh.

43
00:04:05,031 --> 00:04:07,031
I have no idea what my brother was thinking.

44
00:04:09,031 --> 00:04:11,031
Did you pay your fee yet?

45
00:04:11,031 --> 00:04:14,031
The front desk's over there. 5,000 yen.

46
00:04:14,031 --> 00:04:16,031
Good luck. Knock him dead.

47
00:04:16,031 --> 00:04:17,031
See ya.

48
00:04:17,031 --> 00:04:19,031
Oh, wow!

49
00:04:21,031 --> 00:04:23,031
A grass field!

50
00:04:23,031 --> 00:04:27,031
I can't believe I get to play soccer on such a beautiful field on such a beautiful day!

51
00:04:28,031 --> 00:04:31,031
Man, I wish Shun could see this. He'd love it too!

52
00:04:35,031 --> 00:04:37,031
I'm Date, the head coach.

53
00:04:37,031 --> 00:04:41,031
Some of you may already be aware, but this will be our ninth year in J1.

54
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:44,031
And we've accomplished quite a bit.

55
00:04:44,031 --> 00:04:46,031
Some background on our team.

56
00:04:46,031 --> 00:04:49,031
We've won the league title, and also the Emperor's Cup.

57
00:04:49,031 --> 00:04:51,031
First team's record's solid gold.

58
00:04:51,031 --> 00:04:54,031
It's all because of how well our youth players are trained.

59
00:04:55,031 --> 00:05:00,031
Experience coaching is considered the finest in all Japan, especially for youth.

60
00:05:00,031 --> 00:05:02,031
I'll let you take it from here, Manager Fukuda.

61
00:05:03,031 --> 00:05:06,031
Good to see you guys. Thanks for coming out here today.

62
00:05:06,031 --> 00:05:15,031
A team that fails to nurture the next generation has no future.

63
00:05:15,031 --> 00:05:24,031
Realistically, though, pro soccer clubs end up having to acquire players from other organizations all the time to help balance out any weaknesses on their team.

64
00:05:24,031 --> 00:05:29,031
And then, sometimes, the player ends up being a letdown.

65
00:05:30,031 --> 00:05:31,031
Tragic.

66
00:05:31,031 --> 00:05:34,031
Well, that doesn't happen with players that we've been training ever since they were young.

67
00:05:34,031 --> 00:05:37,031
We know their skills and personalities better than anyone.

68
00:05:37,031 --> 00:05:40,031
We understand their strengths and weaknesses.

69
00:05:41,031 --> 00:05:43,031
These benefits can all be yours as well.

70
00:05:43,031 --> 00:05:46,031
Training with us will allow you to absorb the club's style of play.

71
00:05:46,031 --> 00:05:49,031
That's what it means when we say we raise players.

72
00:05:49,031 --> 00:05:52,031
We believe the future of Japanese soccer lies there.

73
00:05:53,031 --> 00:05:55,031
If you pass today, then we'll work together.

74
00:05:56,031 --> 00:05:57,031
And if you don't, use it.

75
00:05:58,031 --> 00:06:00,031
Use this experience to help grow and become a better player.

76
00:06:01,031 --> 00:06:04,031
Then come back and laugh at us for not seeing your potential.

77
00:06:07,031 --> 00:06:08,031
Let's go!

78
00:06:08,031 --> 00:06:11,031
That sounded good. What'd you think, Benzin?

79
00:06:11,031 --> 00:06:14,031
If it was good, then you just ruined it.

80
00:06:15,031 --> 00:06:16,031
Aw, crap!

81
00:06:16,031 --> 00:06:19,031
I barely know anything about the J League or youth teams.

82
00:06:19,031 --> 00:06:21,031
Or this club, for that matter.

83
00:06:21,031 --> 00:06:24,031
I only came to this thing because he asked me to.

84
00:06:26,031 --> 00:06:30,031
And still, I can't stop freaking out about it.

85
00:06:30,031 --> 00:06:32,031
Ugh, this kinda sucks!

86
00:06:35,031 --> 00:06:37,031
One more thing before we start.

87
00:06:38,031 --> 00:06:41,031
It's rare for us to select new players from these tryouts,

88
00:06:41,031 --> 00:06:43,031
so don't get your hopes up.

89
00:06:43,031 --> 00:06:46,031
Start getting used to the fact that we might not pick any of you.

90
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:47,031
Huh?

91
00:06:48,031 --> 00:06:51,031
Why'd you wait till now to tell us that, old man?

92
00:06:51,031 --> 00:06:53,031
Watch your tone, kid! Show some dare respect!

93
00:06:54,031 --> 00:06:55,031
But it's not fair!

94
00:06:56,031 --> 00:06:59,031
Look how many people came here to try to get in!

95
00:06:59,031 --> 00:07:02,031
And you're saying you might decide not to pick anyone?

96
00:07:02,031 --> 00:07:03,031
That's just wrong!

97
00:07:03,031 --> 00:07:14,031
Ooh, smart mouth's in for it now.

98
00:07:15,031 --> 00:07:18,031
Oh, you're right. I guess I forgot to mention that.

99
00:07:18,031 --> 00:07:19,031
Hm?

100
00:07:19,031 --> 00:07:22,031
Sorry it slipped my mind, Ashito.

101
00:07:22,031 --> 00:07:25,031
Everything piled up and we were running out of time.

102
00:07:25,031 --> 00:07:26,031
My bad!

103
00:07:26,031 --> 00:07:28,031
What? Why is he wearing sandals?

104
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:33,031
This team is managed by a crazy, creepy old man!

105
00:07:33,031 --> 00:07:34,031
What?

106
00:07:34,031 --> 00:07:35,031
What?

107
00:07:35,031 --> 00:07:36,031
What?

108
00:07:36,031 --> 00:07:37,031
What?

109
00:07:37,031 --> 00:07:38,031
What?

110
00:07:38,031 --> 00:07:39,031
What?

111
00:07:39,031 --> 00:07:40,031
What?

112
00:07:40,031 --> 00:07:41,031
What?

113
00:07:41,031 --> 00:07:42,031
What?

114
00:07:42,031 --> 00:07:43,031
What?

115
00:07:43,031 --> 00:07:44,031
This team is not going to play ground soccer.

116
00:07:44,031 --> 00:07:46,031
We only take players who are game-ready.

117
00:07:46,031 --> 00:07:47,031
Look.

118
00:07:47,031 --> 00:07:49,031
Last year, with all the players one year above you,

119
00:07:49,031 --> 00:07:51,031
we added 15 players to the team.

120
00:07:51,031 --> 00:07:53,031
Of these only three of them were scouted.

121
00:07:53,031 --> 00:07:55,031
We only found one at tryouts.

122
00:07:55,031 --> 00:07:57,031
And the rest were promoted from the junior youth team.

123
00:07:57,031 --> 00:07:59,451
Promoted? I didn't know that.

124
00:07:59,851 --> 00:08:06,871
Yeah. I'd say most of the time over half of our youth team is made up of players who were doing very well on the junior youth team.

125
00:08:07,751 --> 00:08:13,051
Last year, we had 25 third-year students working out on our junior youth team alone.

126
00:08:13,771 --> 00:08:18,011
That means 14 hard-working kids believed they'd be promoted, and they were not.

127
00:08:18,771 --> 00:08:20,551
Then we have the scouted players.

128
00:08:21,551 --> 00:08:26,051
Talon scouts are always buzzing around Tokyo's soccer fields looking for the next star player.

129
00:08:27,031 --> 00:08:33,391
If we discover someone worthwhile, we'll negotiate directly with that kid to join the team right then and there.

130
00:08:33,931 --> 00:08:37,531
Oh, so you're saying I wasn't worthwhile to you, you lame old geezer?

131
00:08:38,151 --> 00:08:43,631
Basically, our scouts have done all the work needed to find the best players, and you were not among them.

132
00:08:44,251 --> 00:08:49,831
86 of you here were initially passed on. 86 of you who weren't worth an immediate negotiation.

133
00:08:51,171 --> 00:08:54,171
That's really harsh, man. Why are you saying it like that?

134
00:08:54,311 --> 00:08:54,971
Fook it out.

135
00:08:54,971 --> 00:08:59,951
But here's the thing. This doesn't come as a surprise to any of you, does it?

136
00:09:00,591 --> 00:09:04,931
You know you're not there yet, but you still came to take a chance on a slim possibility.

137
00:09:05,891 --> 00:09:11,031
So many of you want to join Tokyo City Asperion. Bad enough, you still showed up.

138
00:09:11,951 --> 00:09:16,851
Players with passion strong enough to change their game really do shine through in a crowd like this.

139
00:09:16,851 --> 00:09:21,511
That kind of spark is essential to this club. It's a spirit of defiance.

140
00:09:22,031 --> 00:09:26,891
A player who will be determined to turn tables. Man, I'd kill to have players like that.

141
00:09:27,631 --> 00:09:30,311
Light that spark today, and we will find our way to you.

142
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:32,971
Show us what you got.

143
00:09:32,971 --> 00:09:43,471
First things first, we need each one of you to take this fitness test.

144
00:09:48,591 --> 00:09:50,051
6.01.

145
00:09:50,051 --> 00:09:54,611
Bro, why are you shaking?

146
00:09:58,511 --> 00:10:00,151
Whoa, looks like I am, too.

147
00:10:00,931 --> 00:10:03,231
Oh, my stomach hurts when I'm nervous.

148
00:10:03,771 --> 00:10:04,471
Owie.

149
00:10:04,471 --> 00:10:09,111
You're the first other candidate to speak to me since I got here. Congrats!

150
00:10:10,211 --> 00:10:13,871
I'm Ashito Aoi. My position is Genius Forward.

151
00:10:14,851 --> 00:10:16,111
I'm Esaku Otomo.

152
00:10:17,231 --> 00:10:20,571
But I don't care about your name. You're ruining everything for me.

153
00:10:21,371 --> 00:10:21,711
Huh?

154
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,751
You couldn't keep your stupid mouth shut.

155
00:10:23,891 --> 00:10:26,691
So manager Fukuda decided to give us that fluffy speech.

156
00:10:26,891 --> 00:10:28,291
And now these losers are fired up.

157
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:31,451
At first, they were shaking like the autumn leaves out there.

158
00:10:31,451 --> 00:10:34,391
I actually had a chance to psych those guys out.

159
00:10:35,171 --> 00:10:36,831
Oh, is that so?

160
00:10:37,491 --> 00:10:37,731
Hmm?

161
00:10:39,491 --> 00:10:42,091
You're right. We were all nervous when we got here.

162
00:10:42,511 --> 00:10:44,811
But I think it'll be even more fun this way.

163
00:10:45,011 --> 00:10:45,271
Huh?

164
00:10:46,351 --> 00:10:49,631
I get to play soccer with all of these guys at their best.

165
00:10:52,951 --> 00:10:57,171
Next, we'll do 20-minute games.

166
00:10:57,511 --> 00:10:58,831
Teams of seven-on-seven.

167
00:10:58,831 --> 00:11:01,271
The most important part of the first stage.

168
00:11:01,451 --> 00:11:03,051
Good luck out there, everybody.

169
00:11:04,311 --> 00:11:07,151
What the hell kind of moron put these teams together?

170
00:11:08,231 --> 00:11:09,791
This is so unfair.

171
00:11:11,591 --> 00:11:12,811
Bring it on.

172
00:11:12,811 --> 00:11:25,691
Hey there, big brother!

173
00:11:26,231 --> 00:11:27,311
How's the grading going?

174
00:11:28,171 --> 00:11:32,191
Hana, I told you not to call me that when we're on the field.

175
00:11:32,531 --> 00:11:33,391
Oh, right.

176
00:11:33,931 --> 00:11:35,131
Sorry about that, sir.

177
00:11:35,511 --> 00:11:36,431
Hey, listen, Hana.

178
00:11:36,831 --> 00:11:39,011
I didn't realize it was going to be so hot out here.

179
00:11:39,831 --> 00:11:42,371
You're the manager's sister, so feel free to take a break.

180
00:11:42,431 --> 00:11:42,751
It's cool.

181
00:11:44,671 --> 00:11:47,331
I'm sure it's a whole lot worse for all the guys out there.

182
00:11:47,931 --> 00:11:49,231
Their careers are on the line.

183
00:11:49,231 --> 00:11:53,811
Although, not all of them seem to be talented.

184
00:11:54,811 --> 00:11:56,511
It feels very one-sided.

185
00:11:56,511 --> 00:12:16,331
Hey, what are you doing?

186
00:12:16,891 --> 00:12:18,331
Quit the ball hogging.

187
00:12:18,551 --> 00:12:20,771
You're not the only one playing this game, Ehime.

188
00:12:21,011 --> 00:12:22,491
Stop giving the ball away.

189
00:12:22,731 --> 00:12:25,751
What am I supposed to do when none of you will pass me the ball?

190
00:12:26,011 --> 00:12:27,591
All I want to do is score.

191
00:12:27,911 --> 00:12:30,831
And since you won't pass it to me, I have to take it upfield myself.

192
00:12:30,991 --> 00:12:33,411
No one's passing it to you because you never passed back.

193
00:12:33,531 --> 00:12:35,971
You come out here yapping about how genius of a player you are,

194
00:12:36,071 --> 00:12:38,431
but you're just another annoying, obnoxious show-off.

195
00:12:38,431 --> 00:12:45,151
You make big moves, and I can respect that.

196
00:12:45,611 --> 00:12:47,311
It's not entirely your fault.

197
00:12:48,251 --> 00:12:49,331
We're pure chaos.

198
00:12:49,551 --> 00:12:50,651
Our teamwork sucks.

199
00:12:51,371 --> 00:12:52,571
We need to pull it together.

200
00:12:54,331 --> 00:12:56,711
Looks like they've got some trouble on the white team.

201
00:12:58,291 --> 00:12:59,891
That doesn't surprise me one bit.

202
00:13:00,071 --> 00:13:01,531
They're getting eaten alive out there.

203
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:05,611
That's how Ichiro Tachibana kid is outshining them all.

204
00:13:05,991 --> 00:13:07,391
What the heck was that?

205
00:13:08,011 --> 00:13:10,351
Rumor has it that these tryouts are just for show,

206
00:13:10,531 --> 00:13:14,191
and the real reason behind them is to work out whether or not to sign him up right away.

207
00:13:16,291 --> 00:13:16,771
Nice!

208
00:13:17,071 --> 00:13:18,391
I'm free over here!

209
00:13:19,271 --> 00:13:20,331
Hey, I'm free!

210
00:13:23,831 --> 00:13:24,531
What the?

211
00:13:25,111 --> 00:13:26,411
Don't worry, Kaneda.

212
00:13:26,411 --> 00:13:27,931
It was a nice try!

213
00:13:31,531 --> 00:13:34,031
Yo, bro.

214
00:13:34,611 --> 00:13:37,431
Is it normal to have such a huge skill gap between the teams?

215
00:13:37,891 --> 00:13:38,111
Hmm?

216
00:13:38,791 --> 00:13:39,171
Hmph.

217
00:13:40,251 --> 00:13:42,391
These tryouts aren't about entire teams.

218
00:13:42,771 --> 00:13:44,491
Individual careers are at stake here.

219
00:13:44,851 --> 00:13:48,271
They're all fighting to stand out and be better than the guy next to them.

220
00:13:48,591 --> 00:13:50,251
It's all me, me, me.

221
00:13:50,911 --> 00:13:53,991
Being thrown into a makeshift team where no one knows each other

222
00:13:53,991 --> 00:13:56,851
makes it near impossible to show off one's A-game.

223
00:13:57,031 --> 00:13:59,151
They're serving their own needs in the moment,

224
00:13:59,151 --> 00:14:02,991
wondering which role to play in this unusual and imperfect situation.

225
00:14:03,711 --> 00:14:07,211
The thing is, we aren't judging their physicality or techniques.

226
00:14:08,191 --> 00:14:11,511
We're judging their ability to think, their intelligence.

227
00:14:12,651 --> 00:14:13,871
That kid from A-Hime?

228
00:14:14,251 --> 00:14:14,951
He's done.

229
00:14:15,431 --> 00:14:17,371
He's just completely frozen on the field.

230
00:14:17,371 --> 00:14:20,371
I don't know what manager Fukuda was thinking having him come out.

231
00:14:20,591 --> 00:14:21,351
He's worthless.

232
00:14:26,871 --> 00:14:27,551
Damn it.

233
00:14:28,011 --> 00:14:29,691
Why can't I stop doing this?

234
00:14:29,911 --> 00:14:32,371
But you're just another annoying, obnoxious show-off!

235
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:39,331
I'm used to being on a team with friends, people who know me,

236
00:14:39,731 --> 00:14:41,571
and they'd let me play the way that I wanted.

237
00:14:42,531 --> 00:14:46,071
As long as I live, I will never forget that.

238
00:14:48,351 --> 00:14:50,991
But playing with these guys is something else.

239
00:14:51,511 --> 00:14:52,911
They've all got their own skills.

240
00:14:53,511 --> 00:14:54,791
It'll be harder to beat them.

241
00:14:54,791 --> 00:14:57,551
Real soccer players.

242
00:14:58,011 --> 00:14:59,051
Ruthless strategies.

243
00:14:59,711 --> 00:15:01,971
This is what soccer should feel like!

244
00:15:20,471 --> 00:15:21,191
Yes.

245
00:15:21,751 --> 00:15:22,231
Otomo!

246
00:15:22,231 --> 00:15:22,471
Otomo!

247
00:15:24,791 --> 00:15:29,151
Does he know how to play this game?

248
00:15:29,611 --> 00:15:32,551
He's a forward, but he dropped all the way into defense for some reason.

249
00:15:33,111 --> 00:15:36,991
I seriously hope he's not trying to make a grandstand play this late in the game.

250
00:15:37,051 --> 00:15:38,271
Is your brain working, A-Hime?

251
00:15:38,451 --> 00:15:38,971
Come on!

252
00:15:39,071 --> 00:15:40,171
Pass it back to me!

253
00:15:40,331 --> 00:15:41,271
What's wrong with you?

254
00:15:41,331 --> 00:15:42,951
The ball's way too close to our goal.

255
00:15:43,111 --> 00:15:43,511
Move!

256
00:15:43,711 --> 00:15:44,811
Don't leave with regrets!

257
00:15:44,971 --> 00:15:47,151
You all only got five minutes to go!

258
00:15:49,771 --> 00:15:50,571
Almost there!

259
00:15:50,831 --> 00:15:51,791
I can do this!

260
00:15:52,131 --> 00:15:53,771
Sucks he came all the way from A-Hime.

261
00:15:53,771 --> 00:15:56,311
Eh, there's no way he's making the cut after that.

262
00:15:57,911 --> 00:15:58,511
Dammit!

263
00:15:58,951 --> 00:16:00,891
What the heck is that freak doing?

264
00:16:00,891 --> 00:16:13,091
Come on!

265
00:16:13,091 --> 00:16:14,511
I'm begging you!

266
00:16:14,511 --> 00:16:17,071
Take one more step in this direction!

267
00:16:17,071 --> 00:16:18,491
This is insane.

268
00:16:18,911 --> 00:16:21,131
Why is A-Hime holding the ball in that area?

269
00:16:21,591 --> 00:16:23,631
He better have some wicked move coming up.

270
00:16:25,391 --> 00:16:27,011
Check out Captain Crazy Hair.

271
00:16:27,251 --> 00:16:28,731
Is that a panic attack or what?

272
00:16:28,931 --> 00:16:29,251
Yeah.

273
00:16:29,911 --> 00:16:31,911
If we apply pressure, we can take it.

274
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:32,791
Let's go!

275
00:16:32,791 --> 00:16:42,251
What's wrong with him?

276
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,991
Why is he dribbling towards his own goal?

277
00:16:44,551 --> 00:16:45,911
Kaneda, get going!

278
00:16:45,911 --> 00:16:59,531
Ethan!

279
00:16:59,531 --> 00:16:59,651
Ethan!

280
00:17:03,651 --> 00:17:04,011
Awesome!

281
00:17:04,011 --> 00:17:05,431
Way to be there, Kaneda!

282
00:17:05,431 --> 00:17:06,731
That was me!

283
00:17:06,931 --> 00:17:08,571
I'm the one who told him to start running!

284
00:17:08,691 --> 00:17:10,771
If I hadn't, you wouldn't have moved, right?

285
00:17:10,971 --> 00:17:11,231
Huh?

286
00:17:11,571 --> 00:17:11,931
Hey!

287
00:17:12,291 --> 00:17:13,631
Did you guys see that?

288
00:17:14,171 --> 00:17:16,431
I'm the guy who shines even when he doesn't score!

289
00:17:16,631 --> 00:17:17,711
Name's Ashito Aoi!

290
00:17:17,791 --> 00:17:18,491
Remember it!

291
00:17:18,611 --> 00:17:19,791
Aoi, Aoi, Aoi, Aoi!

292
00:17:20,211 --> 00:17:22,231
Well, I didn't really expect that to work.

293
00:17:22,311 --> 00:17:23,251
It was pure luck.

294
00:17:24,071 --> 00:17:24,271
Hm.

295
00:17:24,271 --> 00:17:27,511
I gotta admit, assists feel great.

296
00:17:28,951 --> 00:17:29,111
Oh?

297
00:17:32,331 --> 00:17:32,811
Hm.

298
00:17:34,571 --> 00:17:35,011
Hm.

299
00:17:36,291 --> 00:17:37,831
That was so amazing!

300
00:17:38,191 --> 00:17:39,611
I can't even believe it was real!

301
00:17:40,031 --> 00:17:41,751
Such brilliant timing, wasn't it?

302
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:46,551
As the forward, he dropped all the way into his own end of the field to bait the opposition.

303
00:17:47,111 --> 00:17:48,811
Even their defenders left the goal!

304
00:17:49,471 --> 00:17:52,351
That created an opening on the other end for a fraction of a second,

305
00:17:52,351 --> 00:17:54,771
and then he sent a long pass upfield!

306
00:17:55,451 --> 00:17:57,611
And it glided with pinpoint precision!

307
00:17:58,271 --> 00:18:00,131
That play told me who he was.

308
00:18:00,311 --> 00:18:04,051
It's just like I got a bird's eye view of his perspective of the entire soccer field!

309
00:18:06,931 --> 00:18:08,151
And time's up.

310
00:18:09,011 --> 00:18:12,371
We'll now decide which eleven of you will move on to the next round.

311
00:18:18,191 --> 00:18:20,731
I've never seen anyone eat as much as you do.

312
00:18:20,731 --> 00:18:21,231
Hm.

313
00:18:21,931 --> 00:18:24,331
I don't understand why you're not eating anything.

314
00:18:24,411 --> 00:18:27,831
The food won't stay down, because I'm too nervous about whether or not I made it.

315
00:18:28,331 --> 00:18:31,151
I didn't get any time on the ball to show him what I can do.

316
00:18:31,371 --> 00:18:32,031
Like at all.

317
00:18:33,411 --> 00:18:34,831
So Ichiro Tachibana,

318
00:18:35,251 --> 00:18:36,251
Akinori Kanida,

319
00:18:36,831 --> 00:18:37,771
Yudai Hasegawa,

320
00:18:38,111 --> 00:18:39,091
and Lee Yong-suk.

321
00:18:39,471 --> 00:18:41,391
I think all of these guys are strong choices.

322
00:18:43,151 --> 00:18:45,251
Tsukishima, what are your thoughts so far?

323
00:18:45,251 --> 00:18:46,831
Aisaku Otomo!

324
00:18:47,471 --> 00:18:49,091
I thought he was very unique.

325
00:18:49,431 --> 00:18:50,451
I remember that guy,

326
00:18:50,811 --> 00:18:53,711
but I don't remember him making any moves that stood out to me.

327
00:18:53,891 --> 00:18:57,071
Yeah, but I was thinking of his behavior both on and off the field.

328
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:58,711
Do you guys know what I mean?

329
00:18:58,871 --> 00:18:59,731
I suppose.

330
00:18:59,931 --> 00:19:00,411
Me too.

331
00:19:01,131 --> 00:19:02,951
Even before the tryouts got underway,

332
00:19:03,231 --> 00:19:05,671
he was going around chatting up his competitors.

333
00:19:06,131 --> 00:19:08,691
He seemed rather focused on the white jerseys,

334
00:19:08,851 --> 00:19:11,191
especially the ones with numbers closest to his.

335
00:19:11,471 --> 00:19:12,431
Do you get it?

336
00:19:12,431 --> 00:19:15,751
He picked out guys who were most likely to be teammates for the minigame.

337
00:19:15,871 --> 00:19:17,531
Focused his attention on them

338
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:20,811
so he could gauge personalities and playing styles in advance.

339
00:19:21,191 --> 00:19:22,511
I don't know about that.

340
00:19:23,171 --> 00:19:23,931
I do.

341
00:19:24,491 --> 00:19:26,211
I'm telling you, he'll be worth it.

342
00:19:26,551 --> 00:19:28,031
Trust me, he's a shrewd one.

343
00:19:28,191 --> 00:19:31,251
Also, he's the only one I saw trying to motivate his team

344
00:19:31,251 --> 00:19:33,511
when the chips were down and the stakes were high.

345
00:19:34,291 --> 00:19:36,611
All I know is we're short on midfielders.

346
00:19:37,311 --> 00:19:37,951
We'll keep him.

347
00:19:38,571 --> 00:19:41,251
The biggest question mark is Ashito Aoi.

348
00:19:41,251 --> 00:19:44,171
Hey, seems like collectively we're quite split on him.

349
00:19:52,811 --> 00:19:54,151
Wait, it's you.

350
00:19:54,631 --> 00:19:55,451
I'm sorry.

351
00:19:55,711 --> 00:19:57,331
I didn't realize you were the lunch lady.

352
00:19:57,611 --> 00:19:57,971
What?

353
00:19:58,091 --> 00:19:58,711
I'm not.

354
00:19:58,891 --> 00:20:00,931
You just saw me helping out at tryouts.

355
00:20:01,151 --> 00:20:02,531
I'm volunteering here today.

356
00:20:02,931 --> 00:20:04,791
We're probably the same age, too.

357
00:20:04,791 --> 00:20:06,391
Stop distracting me.

358
00:20:06,571 --> 00:20:07,731
No more seconds for you.

359
00:20:07,871 --> 00:20:08,131
What?

360
00:20:09,351 --> 00:20:10,611
Don't act so surprised.

361
00:20:10,831 --> 00:20:13,651
If you make the cut, then you'll have to play another game right away.

362
00:20:14,071 --> 00:20:16,611
And on top of that, you've had plenty of fried food already,

363
00:20:16,771 --> 00:20:18,731
which is hard to digest and will only slow you down.

364
00:20:18,731 --> 00:20:25,831
Hey, it doesn't make any sense for a reckless guy like you to think that far ahead.

365
00:20:26,191 --> 00:20:27,951
I doubt you could pull off a pass like that.

366
00:20:28,671 --> 00:20:29,291
Tell the truth.

367
00:20:29,751 --> 00:20:30,991
Was it just a dumb accident?

368
00:20:30,991 --> 00:20:36,171
To be honest with you, I'm not exactly sure myself.

369
00:20:37,271 --> 00:20:39,671
They'd completely owned us up until that point.

370
00:20:39,951 --> 00:20:43,451
So I stopped and looked around the field, trying to come up with something to do.

371
00:20:43,451 --> 00:20:49,931
It's a weird habit of mine, but looking around the field calms me down.

372
00:20:50,671 --> 00:20:52,771
I don't really remember much after that.

373
00:20:53,391 --> 00:20:55,951
My body just sort of reacted to it.

374
00:20:56,191 --> 00:20:57,011
That's awesome!

375
00:20:57,231 --> 00:20:58,411
So it was intuition!

376
00:20:59,151 --> 00:20:59,411
Hmm?

377
00:21:00,211 --> 00:21:01,551
I'm so relieved.

378
00:21:01,731 --> 00:21:04,531
I knew it wasn't something a normal teenager could copy.

379
00:21:05,191 --> 00:21:05,611
What?

380
00:21:06,411 --> 00:21:09,451
My all-time favorite player said the game was always right there.

381
00:21:09,911 --> 00:21:12,011
Whatever he was doing, soccer was on his mind.

382
00:21:12,011 --> 00:21:15,591
During training, during a match, even when he wasn't playing.

383
00:21:16,071 --> 00:21:17,591
Like it was baked into his soul.

384
00:21:17,971 --> 00:21:19,431
He never stopped thinking about it.

385
00:21:20,111 --> 00:21:21,251
Nothing was more important.

386
00:21:23,271 --> 00:21:27,851
When something's completely part of you like that, it comes naturally, without having to think.

387
00:21:28,471 --> 00:21:32,471
He believed that feeling was the indication that you've truly mastered your craft.

388
00:21:33,111 --> 00:21:36,171
He'd say it's similar to intuition, but not quite the same thing.

389
00:21:37,911 --> 00:21:38,911
Best of luck.

390
00:21:39,531 --> 00:21:41,671
And remember, a man is but a thinking reed.

391
00:21:42,771 --> 00:21:44,411
Hi, I'm Hana Ichijo.

392
00:21:44,591 --> 00:21:45,251
Nice to meet you.

393
00:21:45,651 --> 00:21:47,071
I'm manager Fukuda's sister.

394
00:21:47,491 --> 00:21:48,191
Step-sister.

395
00:21:49,571 --> 00:21:49,871
Hmm.

396
00:21:50,591 --> 00:21:50,831
Hmm.

397
00:21:55,731 --> 00:21:56,011
Goal!

398
00:21:57,011 --> 00:22:00,111
23-year-old Tatsuya Fukuda is unstoppable!

399
00:22:00,771 --> 00:22:05,051
He just sent a laser beam of a long pass upfield from inside his team's end!

400
00:22:05,051 --> 00:22:09,271
Good afternoon, candidates.

401
00:22:09,271 --> 00:22:27,071
May I have your attention, please?

402
00:22:27,071 --> 00:22:31,111
We have made our decision on who will move on to the next stage.

403
00:22:31,111 --> 00:22:34,031
If your name is called, please make your way to the field.

404
00:22:34,031 --> 00:22:34,091
Thank you.

405
00:22:34,091 --> 00:22:34,211
Thank you.

406
00:22:34,211 --> 00:22:34,691
Thank you.

407
00:22:34,691 --> 00:22:35,791
Thank you.

408
00:22:35,791 --> 00:22:36,251
Thank you.

409
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,446
Next time on Awashi, the final test begins.

